Agent Response: Thanks — a few quick points and then how I can help.

1) SSNs don’t expire, so you don’t need to worry about an “expiry date” for the SSN itself. Also, please avoid sharing full SSNs in chat or other insecure places.

2) I assume you mean the passport expiry (or possibly the visa’s expiry). Common rules:
- Many countries (and many airlines) require your passport to be valid for at least six months beyond your planned date of departure/entry. 
- For a six‑month visa/stay, your passport should generally be valid through the entire visa period — and in many cases also for six months after your planned departure. 
- If the passport expires within those six months, you should renew before traveling.

3) How to check for your case (quick checklist):
